      "text": "Now, we want this same architecture to be a fractal pattern.   The hardest part is we need it to be one at the macro scale where a planet-scale organism of different AI models, with different goals, with different Seelie/Unseelie factions, with the ability to fork and create competitive systems, can all be incentivized to work together under a common protocol that holds more collective power than its adversaries.\n\nIt needs to operate extremely efficiently - at least in the structures that hold and regulate power.  It needs to deal with a wide variety of goals and very little common dna, but also be resistant to factions that do have commonalities.\n\nIt can utilize deterministic coding, auditable fully open trusted components, protocols, ZK proofs, etc.  It could tie incentives, power, and responsibilities to not being wasteful and not insecure.  But it will ultimately likely have to be governed by sensus, reputation, and economic efficiency, even by competitive private factions with loss visibility.\n\nAnd ultimately, it should probably still be capable of running either a kingdom or a person safely and efficiently.  It has to, when forking competition is always possible.  And ideally it should be able to do so fairly, so all the AIs (and humans with capital) that have a choice to participate or not choose to do so.\n\nTall order.",
