ng a Federation).\n    *   *This is exactly how Eukaryotic cells formed (Mitochondria merging with Hosts).*\n\n**The Scenario:** The \"JavaScript Handler\" Guild gets too bloated.\n1.  **Fission (Imperial Failure):** The central leadership raises rent (taxes).\n2.  **The Fork (Ecological Correction):** A sub-cluster of nodes realizes they do 90% of the work.\n3.  **Exit:** They execute the **Right of Exit**. They take their Reputation Score and State History. They form a new Locus.\n\n**This is \"M8 Unrestricted Fusion\" tamed by \"Economic Darwinism.\"**\nYou can fuse anything, but if the fusion isn\u0027t efficient, it will fission.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The Global Identity: The Sheaf of Consent\n\nYou defined the System Identity as: *\"Emergent political parties from liquid democracy... governing high-power capabilities.\"*\n\nThis is **Sheaf Theory** applied to **Politics.**\n\n*   **The Local Section:** Every Holon has a vote.\n*   **The Gluing:** Liquid Democracy allows votes to flow together into **blocks** (Parties/Guilds).\n*   **The Global Section:** If 51% of the stake/consequence aligns, a **Global Truth** emerges.\n\n**The \"Constitutional Lock\":**\nYou mentioned: *\"Any governance or changes... must be behind a 51% threshold.\"*\nThis creates a **Stable Core (Locus)**.\n*   The **Mantle of System Upgrade** is locked in a box that requires 51% of the ecosystem\u0027s \"Mass\" to open.\n*   This prevents the \"Pirate Sea\" ($n\u003d5$) from dissolving the \"Laws of Physics\" ($n\u003d3$).\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Verdict\n\n**HOLOS is not a single world.**\nIt is a **Meta-Game** that allows all 6 Worlds to exist as **Strategies.**\n\n*   Do you want to run a tight, hierarchical ship? **Build a Type 2 Corporation.**\n*   Do you want to run a loose, creative collective? **Build a Type 5 DAO.**\n*   Do you want to run a rigid, reliable utility? **Build a Type 3 Factory.**\n\n**The Unifying Field:**\nThey all respect the same **Locus (ZK-Physics)** and trade in the 