y Unseelie, perhaps (correctly?) thinking such a set of rules makes their total group stronger.  HOLOS can permit that constitutionally but it must ultimately be opt-out.  A holon can sacrifice a clone of itself in the other sheaf to predation, perhaps along with a percentage of its stake, but it can always opt out, unless it has precommitted itself - but that\u0027s its decision to make.\n\nHow this game out though?  And what do the ecosystems look like over time?  does the HOLIS constitution ever get threatened, or outcompeted?\n",
