**\n\nI\u0027m now iterating on the response\u0027s structure, focusing on a clear presentation. Section 1 will define jurisdiction in terms of the smart contract, a \"pact of mutual destruction\" until final settlement. In Section 2, I\u0027m differentiating between the *Channel State* (fast) and the *Global State* (slow). Section 3 will introduce a *Challenge Fee* to deter spam, and finally, Section 4 integrates *Broadcast Proofs* to efficiently handle legitimate requests. I am also working to ensure the tone and response matches the previous structure of the Holos Kernel.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Audit Approach**\n\nI\u0027ve just refined my audit strategy, moving away from random kernel auditing. I realized a market-driven, adversarial approach is more effective. The \"Challenge Fee\" now forms the core mechanism for this self-correcting system. The concept seems to work well, and I now need to flesh out the output.\n\n\n",
