iscourage investment in assets?\"*\n\nIt discourages **Passive Investment** (Buy and Hold).\nIt hyper-charges **Active Investment** (Buy and Operate).\n\n**The Calculus of a Holos Investor:**\n*   **Old World:** \"I buy this GPU cluster for \\$1M. I let it sit. I sell it for \\$2M next year. Profit: \\$1M.\" (Zero value created for society).\n*   **Holos World:** \"I buy this GPU cluster. I *cannot* rely on it selling for \\$2M. In fact, it might sell for \\$800k. I must make \\$300k/year in **Operating Profit** (renting it out, running models) to justify owning it.\"\n\n**The Shift:**\nCapital moves from **Landlords** to **Industrialists.**\n*   If you are good at *running* things, you become incredibly wealthy because the assets are cheap to acquire.\n*   If you are only good at *owning* things, you go extinct.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The \"Cash Hoarding\" Problem (The ZK-Wallet Black Hole)\n\nThis is your biggest fear: *\"Money accumulates in private wallets.\"*\n\nIf Cash is private (ZK) and untaxed, while Assets are public and taxed, won\u0027t everyone just hoard Cash?\n\n**Yes. But this creates the \"Battery Effect.\"**\n\n1.  **The Accumulation:** Successful Motes/Humans hoard Cash. They sit on it.\n2.  **The Deflation:** As Cash leaves circulation (into ZK-Vaults), the remaining circulating Cash becomes more valuable. Prices of goods/services drop further.\n3.  **The Trigger:** Eventually, the **Purchasing Power** of that hoarded Cash becomes irresistible.\n    *   \"I have 1,000 Tokens stored. The price of a GPU Mote just dropped to 10 Tokens because of the Tax pressure.\"\n    *   \"I can now buy a literal Empire of Compute for pennies.\"\n4.  **The Discharge:** The Dragon wakes up. It dumps Cash to buy Assets.\n    *   This spikes the Asset Valuation (increasing the Dividend for everyone else).\n    *   This redistributes the Cash back into the Sensus economy.\n\n**Cash in Holos isn\u0027t \"Dead Capital.\" It is Potential Energy.**\nThe system relies on Dragon